# Local file links (home URI)

## Resolve values (every time)

Before writing a clickable local link:

1. Read **HOME_FILE_URI** and **HOME_PATH** from the Profile setup (`profile-references.mdc`, Read the Profile setup).
2. If `.env` or either key is missing, stop. Ask the user to run `ag setup`.
3. Vault directories come from the Active profile Output map, not from a hardcoded folder name.

Do not store HOME_FILE_URI or HOME_PATH in this rule. They live in each profile `.env` (gitignored). If this machine's home directory changes, update every profile `.env` that exists.

## Markdown link targets

In `[text](target)`, use **absolute `file://` URIs**. Do **not** use relative paths or `~` in link targets (editors do not expand `~` in links).

Build the target:

`target = HOME_FILE_URI + absolute_path` after stripping `HOME_PATH` from the front of the absolute path.

With `HOME_PATH=/Users/me` and `HOME_FILE_URI=file:///Users/me`, the file `/Users/me/vault/notes.md` becomes `file:///Users/me/vault/notes.md`. The home directory appears exactly once. `file:///Users/me/Users/me/…` means `HOME_PATH` was not stripped.

In templates, `{HOME_FILE_URI}` means that prefix after substitution. Never leave a literal username in a skill, command, or rule.

Generated-artifact example: resolve the kind directory from the Output map, then prefix with `{HOME_FILE_URI}` the same way.

Prose and inline code may still use tilde paths when describing directories. Only **clickable** `[label](…)` targets use `{HOME_FILE_URI}`.

## Session transcripts

Do not build transcript targets from a path template. Use the `uri` the resolver prints (`~/.agents/profiles/default/artifacts/skills-profile-me/resolve-agent-sessions/SKILL.md`). It already follows this rule.

Keep `` `<session-id>` `` in backticks on the same line after the link. Never use a bare session id as the link target.
